From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: resolve consecutive timestamps with one counter heap
 resolve

Every timestamp written outside a render pass was resolved from its Metal
counter heap with its own resolveCounterHeap call, and each call takes about
56 KiB of Metal command allocator memory. vkd3d-proton writes 8192
timestamps in one command buffer: one recording took 526 MiB of allocator
memory (1050 MiB for two), and in a Bodycam match the process footprint
grew past 12 GB within a minute until macOS ran out of memory.

Timestamps that follow each other in the same heap and in the query pool
are now resolved with one call.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c
index 9be3f44..ea53c51 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -375,9 +375,18 @@ end_encoder(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, mtl_command_encoder *encoder)
    mtl_release(encoder);
 
    /* Fold the pending timestamp counter-heap resolves into `cmd_buf` */
-   util_dynarray_foreach(&cmd->ts_resolves, struct kk_ts_resolve, r) {
-      mtl_command_resolve_counter_heap(cmd->metal.cmd_buf, r->heap, r->index,
-                                       1u, r->dst_addr);
+   const struct kk_ts_resolve *r = cmd->ts_resolves.data;
+   const unsigned n =
+      util_dynarray_num_elements(&cmd->ts_resolves, struct kk_ts_resolve);
+   for (unsigned i = 0, count; i < n; i += count) {
+      for (count = 1; i + count < n; count++) {
+         if (r[i + count].heap != r[i].heap ||
+             r[i + count].index != r[i].index + count ||
+             r[i + count].dst_addr != r[i].dst_addr + count * sizeof(uint64_t))
+            break;
+      }
+      mtl_command_resolve_counter_heap(cmd->metal.cmd_buf, r[i].heap,
+                                       r[i].index, count, r[i].dst_addr);
    }
 
    util_dynarray_clear(&cmd->ts_resolves);
